Hello Kevin,

 I think the packrat.lock file should be splitted into two files, as below. The first part is user-specific : a difference between Packrat version, R version, links to repos, is not extremely important for collaborating.  The second part containing the packages versions is extremely important for collaboration.

PackratFormat: 1.4
PackratVersion: 0.4.1.1
RVersion: 3.1.2

Repos: CRAN=http://cran.rstudio.com <http://cran.rstudio.com>,
    BioCsoft=http://bioconductor.org/packages/2.14/bioc <http://bioconductor.org/packages/2.14/bioc>,
    BioCann=http://bioconductor.org/packages/2.14/data/annotation <http://bioconductor.org/packages/2.14/data/annotation>,
    BioCexp=http://bioconductor.org/packages/2.14/data/experiment <http://bioconductor.org/packages/2.14/data/experiment>,
    BioCextra=http://bioconductor.org/packages/2.14/extra <http://bioconductor.org/packages/2.14/extra>

___________ SPLIT HERE __________

Package: abind
Source: CRAN
Version: 1.4-0
Hash: 5007322a6d081332d1d54b077a82bdf0

Package: ....

Stéphane

